@echo off
cd /d "C:\Users\SubratoBiswas\trinamix-conversion-workbench"
echo Cleaning any git locks...
del /f /q ".git\index.lock" 2>nul
del /f /q ".git\HEAD.lock" 2>nul
echo Dropping tracked bytecode...
git rm -r --cached --ignore-unmatch backend/app/__pycache__ backend/app/services/__pycache__ backend/app/parsers/__pycache__
echo Staging...
git add -A
echo Committing (no-op if clean)...
git commit -m "Coded values (LOVs): stop writing values Oracle will reject. Fusion fails an FBDI load when a coded column holds anything outside its accepted list, and the error surfaces hours later as an opaque rejection. The template actually publishes this: 110 columns state their codes in the description ('Contains one of the following values: 1 or 2. If 1, then it indicates Yes. If 2, it indicates No.'), and 51 more name an Oracle lookup type. We were discarding all of it - the parser hardcoded lookup_type=None and never filled allowed_values. New lov_service mines the codes, the per-code meaning, and the POLARITY (Oracle spells out which code means no), so descriptive source text resolves deterministically: 'Stocked in warehouse'->Y, 'not critical'->2, 'Manufactured in house'->1. Polarity is read per column, which matters: REVISION_QTY_CONTROL_CODE is inverted (2=controlled, 1=not), and a hand-written Y/N->1/2 rule would have silently written the wrong code on every row. Enforcement runs on the assembled frame at generate: unresolvable value in an optional column is blanked (an empty optional column loads, an invalid one fails the file); in a REQUIRED column it is left alone and raised as an error rather than guessed at. Columns whose codes live in the customer's instance (lookup_type, no published values) are passed through untouched and flagged - we do not invent codes, and the AI crosswalk is now barred from those columns entirely and has its output validated against the accepted code list. New /coded-values audit endpoint + CodedValuesPanel show exactly what will be written, how each value was decided, and what needs a human, BEFORE you generate. Backfill mines existing templates from their stored descriptions - no re-upload."
echo Pushing...
git push origin main
echo.
echo ====== DONE - Press any key to close ======
pause
